text For now, I decide to take the bag off my shoulder and sit on the floor.
text I then take out a cigarette, stick it in my mouth, and light it.
text @[Tomoya]
text Phew...
text I drag the ashtray on the table closer to me.
text Ahead of it, in the doorway, I see Ushio still standing there and looking at me.
music ~
text @[Tomoya]
text *Sigh*
text My spirits dampen.
text ...This is the worst summer break ever.
text If I knew this was going to happen, I would've just kept working.
text But if I did, then Ushio would've been left here all alone...
music BGM08D.mp3
text @[Tomoya]
text *Sigh*
text I let out yet another deep exhale.
text Where could those two have gone?
text I take another look over the note they left.
text It just says they'll be "out for a while."
text How long is that going to be? Four whole days?
text No, I'm sure they'll be back tonight to check on things.
text I figure I just have to wait it out until then.
text When I flip the sheet over, I see a full four-day schedule written there.
text Below it are two train tickets that have been taped on to the sheet of paper.
text They're express tickets.
text I look up.
